Q5/B0 DURABLE-SCOPE CORRECTION before work starts. The reassigned bead body is now narrower and more permissive than the accepted exact plan.

Current bd-01M184XP908JX51S3ZYFX20HC7 says the deliverable need not be long, lists the original model shortlist, and ends by saying this paperwork answer unblocks Stage B. That is superseded by plan hash b12f79c and the lead audit:

- the current component ledger includes exact code, weights, provider terms, dependencies, containers, codecs, tokenizers/quantizers, privacy/retention, purposes, and owner-only actions, including the revised F0/PySceneDetect/FFmpeg and conditional/HOLD components;
- exact Sherlock records and rights, the two-run timebase repair, and aggregate-only fixtures remain part of B0;
- source/corpus/F0/F1/F2 dispositions remain separate;
- no exact source-film plus human-recall pair is admitted;
- the provisional Q5 table explicitly does NOT close B0.

Please replace the bead body with that exit condition before treating it as executable, or split the component table and Sherlock/admission closure into dependent beads whose parent B0 remains open. In either structure, completing the current short table alone must not close Stage B or unlock C1. No terms acceptance, restricted fetch, participant prose, episode video, dependency, or implementation is authorized.
